    gettext_noop("Use-after-free in the irc plugin when a batched message disconnects the server.")
    gettext_noop("WeeChat uses non-constant time password/hash comparison in the Relay plugin and in TOTP validation.\n<br>\nThis could allow an attacker to guess a password, a hash or a TOTP and bypass relay authentication.")
    gettext_noop("When a DCC file transfer is resumed (option <code>xfer.file.auto_resume</code>, enabled by default), WeeChat sends a DCC RESUME message with the size of the partial file already received, and the remote peer replies with a DCC ACCEPT message containing the position to resume from.\n<br>\nThe position received in DCC ACCEPT is not checked against the position sent by WeeChat, and it replaces it:\n<ul>\n  <li>With a position equal to the file size, the transfer is immediately marked as successfully completed: the truncated partial file is kept as if it was complete, and its temporary suffix (option <code>xfer.file.download_temporary_suffix</code>) is removed.</li>\n  <li>With any other position, the data received is appended to the partial file at the wrong offset, so the file received is corrupted.</li>\n</ul>\nThe transfer is identified only by its port, so a DCC ACCEPT message sent by another IRC user knowing the port can have the same effect.\n<br>\nIn addition, the position received in DCC RESUME and DCC ACCEPT is not parsed strictly: an invalid value is not rejected, and when sending a file, a position greater than or equal to the file size is accepted.")
    gettext_noop("When a batch message is received and one of the messages causes a disconnection from the server, the remaining messages are reading data that is already freed.")
    gettext_noop("When connecting to a remote relay (command <code>/remote</code>), WeeChat sends a handshake request and the remote replies with the password hash algorithm and the number of hash iterations to use for authentication.\n<br>\nThe number of iterations is not checked: a malicious remote, or a man-in-the-middle when the connection is not secured with TLS, can send a huge number of iterations (up to about 2 billion), so that WeeChat is blocked for a very long time while computing the password hash with the algorithm <code>pbkdf2+sha256</code> or <code>pbkdf2+sha512</code>.\n<br>\nWith the fix, the number of iterations must be between 1 and 1000000 (the range allowed in option <code>relay.network.password_hash_iterations</code>), otherwise the handshake fails and WeeChat disconnects from the remote.")
    gettext_noop("When decompressing a websocket frame received from a Relay client with \"api\" protocol and permessage-deflate enabled, WeeChat allocates memory without upper limit.\n<br>\nIn case of highly compressed frame, this can lead to memory exhaustion and the WeeChat process can be killed by the OOM killer.")
    gettext_noop("When dumping Relay data with <code>/debug dump</code> or <code>/debug dump relay</code>, any HTTP request with path_items defined causes an out-of-bounds read.")
    gettext_noop("When queuing data of sending to clients, the Relay plugin builds a partial buffer.\n<br>\nThere is no limit for the allocated buffer.\n<br>\nA malicious unauthenticated client sending PING control frames can can lead to memory exhaustion and the WeeChat process can be killed by the OOM killer.")
    gettext_noop("When receiving a DCC file, the filename built contains the remote nick (the option <code>xfer.file.use_nick_in_filename</code> is on by default).\n<br>\nIf the nick contains special characters, the file could be written outside of the configured download path.\n<br>\nXfer never overwrites existing files, so if a file exists with the same name, a suffix like \".1\" is appended to the filename.")
    gettext_noop("When receiving a DCC file, the filename may contain directory separator that is not the platform-native one (for example \"/\" received on Windows or \"\\\" received on Linux). This separator may be interpreted as a directory separator, so the file could be written outside of the configured download path.\n<br>\nXfer never overwrites existing files, so if a file exists with the same name, a suffix like \".1\" is appended to the filename.")
    gettext_noop("When receiving a text message from a client, the Relay plugin builds a partial buffer until the end of text is found.\n<br>\nThere is no limit for the allocated buffer.\n<br>\nA malicious client sending large amount of data without end of text can lead to memory exhaustion and the WeeChat process can be killed by the OOM killer.")
    gettext_noop("When receiving an HTTP request from a client, the Relay plugin keeps all the header lines received until the end of headers is found.\n<br>\nThere is no limit for the allocated buffer, and this happens before the client is authenticated.\n<br>\nA malicious unauthenticated client sending an unlimited number of header lines can lead to memory exhaustion and the WeeChat process can be killed by the OOM killer.")
    gettext_noop("When receiving data on the socket, the IRC plugin builds a partial message until \"\\r\\n\" is found.\n<br>\nThere is no limit for the allocated message.\n<br>\nA malicious server sending large amount of data without end of message (\"\\r\\n\") can lead to memory exhaustion and the WeeChat process can be killed by the OOM killer.")
    gettext_noop("When receiving part of Xfer chat message, the Xfer plugin builds a partial buffer until the end of message is found.\n<br>\nThere is no limit for the allocated buffer.\n<br>\nA malicious client sending large amount of data without end of message can lead to memory exhaustion and the WeeChat process can be killed by the OOM killer.")
    gettext_noop("When receiving part of websocket frame, HTTP message or HTTP body, the Relay plugin builds a partial buffer until the end of data is found.\n<br>\nThere is no limit for the allocated buffer.\n<br>\nA malicious client sending large amount of data without end of websocket frame or HTTP message/body can lead to memory exhaustion and the WeeChat process can be killed by the OOM killer.")
    gettext_noop("When resuming a DCC file transfer, a peer can start it without user manual acceptance.")
    gettext_noop("When the IRC server sends an empty PREFIX in message 005 and the connection is lost before message 001, the nicks are kept with 1-byte prefixes while the default prefix chars (\"@+\") are restored on reconnection, so that the next prefix set on a nick (for example with message 353) is written out of bounds.\n<br>\nNote: a \"normal\" IRC server should not send an empty PREFIX in message 005, so the problem should be limited to malicious IRC servers.")
    gettext_noop("When writing a log file, a specific char used internally as separator may be used to forge a new path that can be outside the path configured by the option <code>logger.file.path</code>.")
    gettext_noop("With SASL mechanisms <code>scram-sha-1</code>, <code>scram-sha-256</code> and <code>scram-sha-512</code>, the IRC plugin does not properly check the data received from the server:\n<ul>\n  <li>The SASL success (numeric 903 or 907) is accepted even if the server did not send its signature, so the server is not authenticated: a malicious server, or a man-in-the-middle, can impersonate the IRC server without knowing the password.</li>\n  <li>The iteration count is not checked: a malicious server, or a man-in-the-middle, can send a very low iteration count (for example 1), so that the client proof sent by WeeChat makes an offline dictionary attack on the password cheap, or a very high iteration count, so that WeeChat is blocked for a long time while computing the proof.</li>\n  <li>The server nonce is not checked: it must start with the nonce sent by the client, as required by RFC 5802.</li>\n</ul>\nThe purpose of SCRAM is to authenticate both the client and the server without sending the password to the server, so these missing checks defeat the protection expected by users choosing these mechanisms.")
    gettext_noop("With WeeChat ≥ 1.1, you can create a trigger:\n\n<p><pre><code>/trigger add fix_irc_352 modifier \"irc_in_352\" \"${arguments} =~ .* \\*$\" \"/.*//\"</code></pre></p>\n\nWith any older version, there is no simple mitigation, you must upgrade WeeChat.")
    gettext_noop("With WeeChat ≥ 1.1, you can create a trigger:\n\n<p><pre><code>/trigger add irc_dcc_quotes modifier \"irc_in_privmsg\" \"${arguments} =~ ^[^ ]+ :${\\x01}DCC SEND ${\\x22} \" \"/.*//\"</code></pre></p>\n\nWith any older version, there is no simple mitigation, you must upgrade WeeChat.")
    gettext_noop("Write of DCC file received outside of configured download path.")
    gettext_noop("Write of logger file outside of configured path.")
    gettext_noop("Xfer")
    gettext_noop("You can remove all relays of type \"irc\", see <code>/help relay</code>.")
    gettext_noop("You can unload the logger plugin, thus stopping recording of all buffers: <code>/plugin unload logger</code>.")
